From: Emaki contributors <emaki@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] screencopy: expose completed-frame damage to cropped consumers

Copyright (C) 2026 Artur Yakymenko
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-only

Keep full-output capture, the shared manager, request cadence and context lifetime
unchanged. Snapshot reliable normal-buffer damage before publishing each completed
frame. Consumers can skip refreshing a crop that cannot change; first copies,
absent metadata and transformed buffers retain full updates. The query maps logical
item coordinates to the completed buffer and pads for linear filtering.

Protocol damage belongs to the manager, not a capture context. Trust it only while
one context uses that manager; a membership epoch also invalidates frames across
peers joining and leaving between completions. Regional and other-output peers
count too. This keeps existing capture timing and makes concurrent captures refresh
conservatively, with no additional compositor trackers.

